# Codex `config.toml` snippet for afk-bootstrap projects
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The codebase-memory MCP server is already wired into Codex on this host
# (entry: `mcp_servers.codebase-memory-mcp` pointing at
# /home/claude/.local/bin/codebase-memory-mcp). If you ever re-provision
# Codex, re-run:
#
#   codebase-memory-mcp install -y     # auto-detects Codex CLI; writes
#                                     # the [mcp_servers.codebase-memory-mcp]
#                                     # block and AGENTS.override entry
#
# That's the only configuration needed. The server talks to per-project
# graphs under ~/.codex-memory-mcp/, which the afk-bootstrap maintainer
# re-indexes with `mcp__codebase-memory-mcp__index_repository` whenever
# the repos change. For afk-bootstrap projects the names are:
#   home-claude-Projects-genesis-evidence
#   home-claude-Projects-health-flow
#   home-claude-Projects-AI-Ops
#   home-claude-Projects-afk-bootstrap
#   home-claude-Projects-Auto-Test
# (the names are the project argument you pass to search_graph / etc.).
#
# If `codebase-memory-mcp` isn't installed on the host, see
# /home/claude/.claude/skills/codebase-memory/SKILL.md for setup.
